<article class="env-lemma" id="0D9E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D9E">Lemma <span data-tag="0D9E">85.12.9</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/09WE" data-tag="09WE">85.3.3</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An object $K$ of $D(\mathcal{C}_{total})$ is cartesian if and only the canonical map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  g_{n!}K_ n \longrightarrow g_{n!}\mathbf{Z} \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_\mathbf {Z} K  \]
</div>
<p>
 is an isomorphism for all $n$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a sheaf of rings on $\mathcal{C}_{total}$ such that the morphisms $f_\varphi ^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ n \to \mathcal{O}_ m$ are flat for all $\varphi : [n] \to [m]$. Then an object $K$ of $D(\mathcal{O})$ is cartesian if and only if the canonical map 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  g_{n!}K_ n \longrightarrow g_{n!}\mathcal{O}_ n \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_\mathcal {O} K  \]
</div>
<p>
 is an isomorphism for all $n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Proof of (1). Since $g_{n!}$ is exact, it induces a functor on derived categories adjoint to $g_ n^{-1}$. The map is the adjoint of the map $K_ n \to (g_ n^{-1}g_{n!}\mathbf{Z}) \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_\mathbf {Z} K_ n$ corresponding to $\mathbf{Z} \to g_ n^{-1}g_{n!}\mathbf{Z}$ which in turn is adjoint to $\text{id} : g_{n!}\mathbf{Z} \to g_{n!}\mathbf{Z}$. Using the description of $g_{n!}$ given in Lemma <a href="/tag/09WG" data-tag="09WG">85.3.5</a> we see that the restriction to $\mathcal{C}_ m$ of this map is 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bigoplus \nolimits _{\varphi : [n] \to [m]} f_\varphi ^{-1}K_ n \longrightarrow \bigoplus \nolimits _{\varphi : [n] \to [m]} K_ m  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Thus the statement is clear. 
    <p>
      Proof of (2). Since $g_{n!}$ is exact (Lemma <a href="/tag/0D74" data-tag="0D74">85.6.3</a>), it induces a functor on derived categories adjoint to $g_ n^*$ (also exact). The map is the adjoint of the map $K_ n \to (g_ n^*g_{n!}\mathcal{O}_ n) \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_{\mathcal{O}_ n} K_ n$ corresponding to $\mathcal{O}_ n \to g_ n^*g_{n!}\mathcal{O}_ n$ which in turn is adjoint to $\text{id} : g_{n!}\mathcal{O}_ n \to g_{n!}\mathcal{O}_ n$. Using the description of $g_{n!}$ given in Lemma <a href="/tag/0D72" data-tag="0D72">85.6.1</a> we see that the restriction to $\mathcal{C}_ m$ of this map is 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bigoplus \nolimits _{\varphi : [n] \to [m]} f_\varphi ^*K_ n \longrightarrow \bigoplus \nolimits _{\varphi : [n] \to [m]} f_\varphi ^*\mathcal{O}_ n \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ m} K_ m = \bigoplus \nolimits _{\varphi : [n] \to [m]} K_ m  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Thus the statement is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>